WEBVTT

00:00:00.079 --> 00:00:02.180
Open Deployments in Omni Dispatch.

00:00:02.619 --> 00:00:06.199
The Open filter gives you the deployments that are still in progress.

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:09.760
Select Community support deployment and check its status

00:00:09.789 --> 00:00:11.210
and assigned resource counts.

00:00:11.619 --> 00:00:14.720
A wildland contractor could use this view to confirm which

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:16.530
deployment a crew is working under.

00:00:16.759 --> 00:00:19.809
Use Previous day to move to the day you are reviewing.

00:00:20.309 --> 00:00:23.189
This exercise has a crew report on November second.

00:00:23.609 --> 00:00:26.600
Reports this day shows that the entry is Approved and

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.549
totals eleven and a half hours.

00:00:28.949 --> 00:00:33.150
Open the report to check the individual entries and their time ranges and breaks.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:36.080
The fields in this approved report are read-only.

00:00:36.349 --> 00:00:40.899
On the Dispatch Console, open the warehouse exercise and select Command.

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:44.660
The command summary names the commander and shows the structure.

00:00:45.099 --> 00:00:48.160
In this example, Squad Three is in Search Division.

00:00:48.679 --> 00:00:52.830
Use View Squad Three to see the lane assignment and its requirements warning.

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:56.949
A search and rescue dispatcher could use the same view to confirm which

00:00:56.949 --> 00:00:58.490
group a search team is working with.

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:02.030
Check Accountability to see the current check-in indicators.

00:01:02.419 --> 00:01:05.569
Objectives shows the progress of the assigned benchmark.

00:01:05.919 --> 00:01:10.449
The separate Check-In tab shows the timer and last check-in for a tracked entry.

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:13.690
Confirm the entry before using the check-in action.

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:19.070
For documentation tied to the call, open its Records tab and select New Record.

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:22.520
The form list shows the choices available to Dispatch.

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:25.430
This training department shows Callback and Run.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:29.470
The department Records workspace also groups items under Assigned

00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:31.899
to you, Drafts and Returned to you.

00:01:32.319 --> 00:01:36.399
Use the call tab when you need the context of a particular incident, and

00:01:36.399 --> 00:01:38.229
the workspace to review your queue.

